Dataset of crystal structures obtained during the prediction of stable phases in Hf-Ta-C system using [USPEX ](https://https://uspex-team.org/en) evolutionary algorithm [[1](https://https://advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/adfm.202206289)]. Most of the structures exhibit rocksalt crystal structures with different arrangment of Hf and Ta atoms.

The **HfTaC_POSCARS** contains entire set of VASP output files incuding POSCAR, CONTCAR, OUTCAR, vasprun.xml.

This makes it possible to parse it and train the ML model using initial and final coordinates, forces, stresses and energies.

Raw crystal structure data obtained directly from the USPEX prediction for different types of calculations is presented in **HfTaC_USPEX dataset**

---

References

[1]. Nassyrbayev, A. A. Sivkov, Z. Bolatova, and A. Ya. Pak, Large-Scale Synthesis and Applications of Hafnium–Tantalum Carbides,[ Advanced Functional Materials **32**, 2206289 (2022)](https://https://advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/adfm.202206289).